{# PROPOSAL -- for C1 to place in templates/macros. NOT active. NOT loaded by any render harness. #}
{# audit_ref: codex-manager-current-source-audits-20260923-0315 (F_representation_audit item 5) #}
{# targets: .github/README-github.md AND .github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/feature_request.md #}
{# tested: false (manifest reform body-wrapper -> declared blocks is OPEN; C1 wires + byte-parity verifies) #}
{#
   Replaces the body-wrapper templates with a DECLARED block list rendered against a
   PER-KIND format map. This is NOT a verbatim-prose wrapper and NOT per-instance literal
   paste: prose WORDS are data (block.text); every STRUCTURAL marker (fence, kv separator,
   bold marker, blank line, terminators) is looked up by section KIND from `formats`, which
   is sourced from the schema. A block carries only {kind, text} (+ {fields, blank_line_before_close}
   for a frontmatter block).

   params -> declared schema keys (emitted-structural-literals-schema.yaml):
     blocks  -> readme_sections[] / feature_request_sections[] (declared blocks; data)
     formats -> markdown_formats.<kind>.* (per-kind fence/kv_separator/terminator/blank_line/
                prefix/suffix); README and feature_request pass different format sets
   No parameter has a default; no string/number literal appears in the body (formats[b.kind]
   uses the block's own declared kind as the key). Terminal newline is OWNED by this macro:
   the last block's terminator is emitted here, so the render layer adds nothing.
#}
{% macro render_markdown_document(blocks, formats) -%}
{% for b in blocks -%}
{% set fmt = formats[b.kind] -%}
{% if b.fields is defined -%}
{{ fmt.fence }}{{ fmt.terminator }}
{%- for f in b.fields %}{{ f.key }}{{ fmt.kv_separator }}{{ f.raw }}{{ fmt.terminator }}{% endfor -%}
{% if b.blank_line_before_close %}{{ fmt.blank_line }}{% endif -%}
{{ fmt.fence }}{{ fmt.terminator }}
{%- else -%}
{{ fmt.prefix }}{{ b.text }}{{ fmt.suffix }}{{ fmt.terminator }}
{%- endif -%}
{% endfor -%}
{%- endmacro %}
